DOCUMENTATION ARTIFACT -- NOT A STANDALONE APPLIABLE PATCH

This file documents the equivalent in-tree edits that the
prep-source.sh USE_W11=1 stanza performs at DKMS PRE_BUILD time via
sed + awk against the embedded pre-patched radeon source tarball.
The new-file diffs below carry PASTE: placeholders rather than the
literal source bytes for two reasons:

  1. The canonical TU source-of-truth lives at
     mesa-rekit/staged/radeon-palm-gate-dkms/usr/src/
     radeon-palm-gate-1.0/w11-sources/radeon_palm_cs_observer.{c,h};
     duplicating those into a unified-diff patch would
     immediately rot.
  2. The actual DKMS build does NOT apply patches/0006*.patch via
     `patch -p1` -- prep-source.sh's USE_W11=1 stanza copies the
     w11-sources/ files into RADEON_DIR directly and sed/awk-edits
     the Makefile + radeon_drv.c.  This file's role is review +
     future-upstream-submission documentation, not build input.

If a downstream consumer ever needs to apply this as a real
unified-diff patch (e.g. for upstream submission), substitute each
PASTE: placeholder with the verbatim contents of the corresponding
w11-sources/ file at that revision.

------------------------------------------------------------------

From: steinmarder W11 cs-observer track
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] drm/radeon: add radeon-palm-gate CS observer skeleton

Adds a read-only, disabled-by-default Command-Stream observer TU
co-located with the radeon module.  Skeleton scope only: module
init/exit, debugfs root creation, module-param decls, and
no-op-when-disabled emit stubs.  Subsequent W11 patches add the
per-event payload + comm filter + JSONL emission + 4 hook
callsites in radeon_cs.c / evergreen_cs.c.

Per the observer design (steinmarder
src/re/r600/findings/active/2026-05-21-radeon-palm-cs-observer-design.md):
purely diagnostic; no packet-stream mutation, no MMIO writes, no
behaviour change when palm_cs_observer=0 (the default).  Closes the
C-side observability gap that Phase V (steinmarder #327, commit
e1f01a75) discovered: standard kprobes for deqp-vk on 6.18 xanmod
silently bypass radeon_cs_ioctl etc.; the in-radeon-module observer
side-steps that blind spot.

Adds:
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_palm_cs_observer.c
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_palm_cs_observer.h
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/Makefile: build the new TU
  - drivers/gpu/drm/radeon/radeon_drv.c: init + cleanup wire-up

The new TU and header land via the DKMS prep-source.sh USE_W11=1
stanza (copies from w11-sources/) for the same reasons W10 followed
that pattern: the embedded prepatched radeon tarball is the canonical
source-of-truth, and this unified-diff documents the equivalent
in-tree edits for review / future upstream submission.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.7)
